+# R1: replaces stock LengthTruncationRecoveryProcessor (same singleton group
+# "tmax_length_recovery", same _order=5) with a variant that additionally
+# DE-PRIMES the max_tokens repetition loop. Root cause on the weak model:
+# a truncated no-tool narration turn is persisted in full, the model sees its
+# own repeated prose 5-6x in context, and re-primes the identical runaway
+# generation — burning the whole 80-step budget on one task (264/958/1818,
+# all budget_exceeded at 70 msgs). On repeated consecutive truncations this
+# processor drops the runaway narration to a tiny stub (so history stops
+# re-showing the loop text) and escalates to a hard "one Bash command, no
+# prose" directive. First truncation keeps the stock head+tail collapse.
+# Contract-safe: only mutates current event content in on_after_model and
